## Weakest kill if the learned reference is fine

On its own record's terms, **F1 `FAST_SCREEN_NO_SUPPORT` (#19) is the weakest scientific kill**. The record affirmatively limits it to one world, one lineage, two canonical steps, calls it a fast screen rather than structural impossibility, and says it forbids only continuation of those residual candidates. F's −4.536265% is large on that slice and D also violates service, but the evidential breadth is far thinner than the multi-world gates. The C3 oracle-marginals ruling (#15) is also weak if described broadly because later review says it priced a different unilateral object; that is a scope problem independent of whether BASE is collapsed.

