+# CEILING2 execution criterion
+
+The investigation is complete only if the requested report exists and its
+run-backed receipt (a) reproduces the four six-decimal clean-path parity values,
+(b) asserts zero scalar `StepEvaluator.evaluate` calls, (c) contains complete
+12-anchor results at 1.66° and 2.40° for all requested ceilings and support
+levels, and (d) records peak RSS below 5 GB, one Python process, pinned numerical
+threads, per-anchor progress, row caps/exhaustion, timing, and host load.

codex
Two of 12 anchors are complete. Each exhausted 915 rows at support ≤2 and 26,739 at ≤6; peak RSS is 2.233 GiB. The clean searches are moving substantially (377 first-improvement moves per completed anchor), consistent with the corrected fixed-point path.
diff --git a/.scratch/ceiling2/run_ceiling2.py b/.scratch/ceiling2/run_ceiling2.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e7f46255bc27e2e54f71eb59fd60f045225eef0a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.scratch/ceiling2/run_ceiling2.py
@@ -0,0 +1,950 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Clean-path ceiling and coalition-support diagnostic.
+
+Selection rule: every objective comparison for one arm/anchor is made from one
+fresh dense boundary-0 StepEvaluator.  BASE is populated with evaluate_many in
+that evaluator before profiles are read.  Endpoints use one separate fresh
+realised full-48 evaluator and one evaluate_many call.  Scalar evaluate is
+replaced globally by a fail-closed raising stub.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+from collections import Counter
+from dataclasses import dataclass
+from fractions import Fraction
+import gc
+import hashlib
+import importlib.util
+import itertools
+import json
+import math
+import os
+from pathlib import Path
+import resource
+import sys
+import threading
+import time
+from typing import Mapping, Sequence
+
+
+WORKSPACE = Path("/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ceiling2-ws")
